# Verible SystemVerilog lint rule configuration.
# One rule per line. `-rule` disables, `+rule` (or bare `rule`) enables,
# `rule=param` configures. See: verible-verilog-lint --help_rules
#
# This is a pragmatic baseline for a small RTL skeleton — strict enough to
# catch real style problems, relaxed where rules fight a 2-space indent project.

# Enforce explicit, readable structure.
+explicit-parameter-storage-type
+parameter-name-style
+packed-dimensions-range-ordering
+no-trailing-spaces
+module-filename
+endif-comment
+generate-label

# Naming conventions.
+module-parameter
+enum-name-style

# Relax rules that are noisy for compact RTL or conflict with our formatting.
-line-length
-no-tabs
